rota lap 4322, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; threshold plus standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. The reading turned the lap: my own carried-forward Yours said migrate three parseInt sites, and fire's instruction is to LOOK at what a ratchet tells you to cut before cutting it. Reading them found a language disagreeing with itself.
think Opened with the detached cold roster pass (tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh --detach, transcript named by the tool per row 20260908.113404) and read the fire row while it ran.
think My elder ITINERARY block left one Yours: 35 parseInt sites in four rooms with no parse_int.rye symlink, glow/ holding three. Glow is this seat's lane.
think Read the three sites rather than migrating them. glow/expr.rye:209, glow/lower_mutate.rye:39, glow/rune_bounded_trap.rye:87 each parse a Glow SOURCE literal after a digit-run scan, so the only behavior tally/parse_int.rye would add is its leading-zero refusal -- a change to what the language accepts.
think Checked whether a seated law already answers it. glow/tokens.rye accepts any digit run; no foundation, spec, or rule names a leading zero. So the question is unruled.
think Then found the sharper fact: glow/rune_shop_gate.rye:524 already refuses a leading zero and calls it "the house parse law" in its own comment. One file keeps a law fourteen files are subject to.
think Measured the population. Eleven hand-rolled `* 10 + ` accumulators plus three parseInt calls, all counted in PROGRAM position through tools/fixtures/t/tame_style_app_sites.sh so the 79 lines where glow/lower_shop_gate.rye writes parseInt INTO the Rye it emits are read as output rather than calls. Fourteen readers, one refusal.
think Proved both ends on metal rather than by grep, through the modules' own public entries, with vendor/zig-toolchain/zig as RYE_ZIG.
think Chose the gate reading carefully. A ceiling on `permissive` would refuse one of the two lawful rulings, so the gate is `disagreement` = min(strict, permissive): zero when the language agrees, and falling under either answer.
think The cold pass came back guard_red on crushed_index, with standing_equipment red as its cascade. Read the evidence: press/date has no row on docs-geode/press/README.md, from a peer's fold ninety minutes earlier.
think Read the scan instead of the page. Its DEEP branch drops date/archive/yonder with a paragraph of reasoning seated 20260906, and its one-level branch nine lines below never did -- while that paragraph's own sentence claimed to be "the one place in this file that disagreed with it". The repair is one grep -vE in the scan, not a row in a peer's room.
obs A lint ratchet is a fine instrument for an application and a blunt one for a language. Migrating the three sites on touch would have taken Glow from thirteen-against-one to ten-against-four, deepening the split by lint in whatever order laps opened files.
obs The elder naive count is put back in the control to prove the program-position reading load-bearing: under grep -c, the compiler's own emitted text reads as calls the compiler makes.
obs The crushed_index exclusion is proven not to be blindness -- an ordinary living subdirectory beside the folded shelf is still counted on both readings, and with the elder line restored the shelf reads as a member (1 -> 2).
obs No REDS row for either finding: reds_pin_capacity reads rows_that_fit=0, pin_open_rows=13, headroom 24 bytes. Both findings ride on the card and here instead, cited by stamp.
obs Against myself: I copied the new scan into the tracked tree while the cold pass was still running and removed it within the minute. tree_moved=no held, and the near miss was my own.
